{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a copper-catalyzed regio- and stereo-selective hydrosilylation of terminal allenes to produce (E)-allylsilanes. Using a Cu(OAc)2/Xantphos catalyst system, the authors achieved high yields and excellent E-selectivity for both 1,1-disubstituted and monosubstituted allenes. Mechanistic studies and DFT calculations suggest that the E-selectivity is kinetically controlled and influenced by \u03c0-\u03c0 interactions between the ligand and the substrate.",
